          %h2#references References
          %p The original definition is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Leray"}> Jean Leray
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em L’anneau d’homologie d’une représentation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Leray-0.pdf", :title => "PDF"} PDF
          %p
            Subsequent development by Leray, incorporating ideas of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"} Henri Cartan
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Leray"}> Jean Leray
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em L’anneau spectral et l’anneau filtré d’homologie d’un espace localement compact et d’une application continue
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"}> Henri Cartan
            ‘s account of the theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"}> Henri Cartan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Faisceaux sur un espace topologique. I, II
              %p
                numdam:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/SHC_1950-1951__3__A14_0/"} I
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/SHC_1950-1951__3__A15_0/"} II
          %p It refers to a previous exposition of the theory in Exposés 12–17 of the first year (1948/1949), which apparently are not scanned, unlike Exposés 1–11.
          %p Further references:
          %p Section C2 in
          %ul#Johnstone
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"}> Yuri Manin
              ,
              %em Methods of homological algebra
          %p A concise and contemporary overview can be found in
          %ul
            %li#CentazzoVitale04
              C. Centazzo,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+Vitale"} E. M. Vitale
              %em Sheaf theory
              , pp.311-358 in Pedicchio, Tholen (eds.),
              %em Categorical Foundations
              , Cambridge UP 2004. (
              %a{:href => "https://perso.uclouvain.be/enrico.vitale/chapter7.pdf"}> draft
              )
          %p
            With motivation from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"}> Masaki Kashiwara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 332
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Warner12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Garth+Warner"}> Garth Warner
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibrations and Sheaves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1773/20977"} hdl:1773/20977
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://sites.math.washington.edu//~warner/Warner_FIBRATIONS%20AND%20SHEAVES.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Warner-FibrationsAndSheaves.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Schapira23
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"}> Pierre Schapira
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Introduction to Categories and Sheaves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~pierre.schapira/LectNotes/CatShv.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Schapira-Sheaves.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A quick pedagogical introduction with an eye towards the generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Dugger"}> Dan Dugger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sheaves and homotopy theory
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/cech.pdf"} pdf
          %p Classics of sheaf theory on topological spaces are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Roger Godement,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topologie algébrique et théorie des faisceaux
                %a{:href => "http://books.google.fr/books/about/Topologie_alg%C3%A9brique_et_th%C3%A9orie_des_fa.html?id=JVrvAAAAMAAJ"} gBooks
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Grothendieck"}> A. Grothendieck
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tohoku"} Tohoku
          %p Recently, an improvement in understanding the interplay of derived functors (inverse image and proper direct image) in sheaf theory on topological spaces has been exhibited in
          %ul
            %li
              Olaf M. Schnuerer, Wolfgang Sergel,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Proper base change for separated locally proper maps
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1404.7630"} arxiv/1404.7630
        .revisedby
